ugh he  did his best to save her in the end she  sacrificed her own life to save him so  bond lost the woman he loved and not  only that but she died in his arms and  to make things worse bond always felt  horribly guilty and responsible for  Elaine's death while fighting the red  demon bond didn't realize the demons had  more than one heart and that mistake led  to Elaine's death because she sacrificed  her own life to save him bond is so  distraught and oppressed by this  traumatic event that he just doesn't  care about anything anymore  he is immortal so he cannot die no  matter how much damage is inflicted upon  him which means that he is cursed to  live forever with crippling guilt over  what happened to a  he allows himself to be arrested and he  makes no effort to defend himself  because nothing matters to him anymore  depressed and heartbroken bond no longer  has a purpose in life and because he  blames himself for what happened to  Elaine he probably feels that he  deserves to be punished he probably  thinks that he deserves to be locked  away and brutally tortured because he  got to live and become immortal while  the woman he loved lost her life to save  him bond has survivor's guilt he feels  that his life is meaningless and the  only thing that is able to grab his  interest even slightly is meliodas when  the captain of the seven deadly sins  comes to recruit bond bond has no  interest whatsoever but when he realizes  how strong Milly Otis is and that if he  joins he will have the opportunity to  test his strength against Milly Otis  bond decides to join the seven deadly  sins  however the bond that we see at this  time is not the real bond he hides his  deep sadness and despair from his  comrades and he presents himself as just  an eccentric guy who loves fighting  strong opponents and getting very very  drunk without knowing his full backstory  we might mistake bond for a carefree and  immature young guy who only cares about  having a good time and living by his own  rules but in reality bonds heavy  drinking and careless attitude is an  attempt to numb his despair and  heartbreak and his need to keep testing  his strength by facing stronger and  stronger opponents most likely stems  from his resentment or the fact that he  is immortal and cannot die so he is  cursed to live forever without Elaine  and with the terrible guilt he feels  over her death in reality bond keeps  trying to challenge him ally Otis and  other strong fighters because he is  probably hoping that he will eventually  find someone who can actually kill him  and save him from his despair and even  knowing this much we can see that bond  is an interesting and multi-dimensional  character he seems like a fun-loving guy  who enjoyed being reckless getting drunk  fighting and in general having a good  time on the surface bond is basically  the party girl of the seven deadly sins  but beneath the surface he is an  emotional and psychological mess  and this comes into play perfectly when  bond decides to kill meliodas because he  was falsely promised by a goddess that  Elaine will be revived if meliodas dies  bond knows that meliodas saved him when  he recruited him into the seven deadly  sins and gave him some sort of purpose  in life after years of utter depression  and despair melioidosis bonds best  friend and bond admits that aside from  Elaine Mele Otis is the only other  person who truly understands him and yet  bond is so haunted by guilt over what  happened to Elaine that he decides that  killing meliodas his best friend is a  price that he is willing to pay in order  to bring Elaine back thankfully bond  fails to kill Milly auras and as he  realizes the truth behind melioidosis  relationship to Elisabeth and the curse  that has been placed on both of them by  the demon king and the supreme deity  bond is wracked with guilt yet again  this time over the fact that he betrayed  meliodas and tried to kill him for all  these years bond has been so depressed  and heartbroken because the woman he  loved died in his arms but he later  learns that meliodas had to go through  this very same experience with Elisabeth  not once not twice but over a hundred  times bond feels terrible about his own  weakness and his willingness to betray  his best friend just so he could spare  himself the emotional torture of losing  Elaine but Mellie Otis understands how  he feels Mele Otis has lived through  that same hell and he forgives bond  right away it takes some time before  bond can overcome his sense of guilt but  he eventually does he develops and grows  as a character and he eventually comes  full circle now there will be some minor  manga spoilers at this point so just  giving you a quick heads-up right now  after Elaine is revived Bimal aesculus  magic bond actually decides to leave her  and enter purgatory in order to save  Mele Otis's emotions from the demon king  bond goes from trying to kill his best  friend in order to revive Elaine -  leaving Elaine and his other friends and  entering the notoriously treacherous  realm of purgatory knowing full well  that he may never see Elaine or his  other friends again bond is so committed  to helping his friend and making things  right after betraying him in the past  and this to me is truly amazing  character development but we're not done  yet eventually we learn about Vaughn's  backstory and how he grew up he was a  poor boy who had to steal just to  survive and he was brutally mistreated  by society he was beaten abused and he  was almost sold into slavery to a sick  maniac nobleman thankfully bond met Joe  vago a werefox who saved him from the  human traffickers and in general taught  him how to survive and treated him as  his own son because he was aware Fox  Chicago had to assume human form to  avoid being brutally murdered because  the humans considered all Beast men  including we're foxes to be dangerous  monsters in fact Shivaji OHS biological  son was eventually hunted down and  murdered by humans even though he was  just a boy and as a result of this  incident bond lost touch with Zhivago  and he basically lost his only real  mentor and parental figure until he  finally meets him again much later in  life bonds back story is truly  heartbreaking and I am not ashamed to  say that I shed a tear or ten when I  read it in the manga and then again when  I saw it animated in season 2 of the  anime after everything he went through  after being beaten abused and faced with  mistreatment and discrimination on a  daily basis we might expect bond to  become a harsh and cold person we might  expect him to never trust anyone and to  be willing to do whatever it takes to  survive without regard to whether his  actions are good or evil after all if he  was mistreated all his life why should  he treat anyone else with respect and  compassion why shouldn't he just become  a brooding jaded man who is angry at the  world and everyone around him but bond  doesn't become angry and jaded we see  this when he first meets Elaine even  though as a bandit he has a reputation  for being greedy in reality he isn't and  he gives up his quest for the Fountain  of Youth after he meets Elaine because  he fell in love with Elaine and he  decided that being with her is much more  important than immortality when he loses  Elaine bond does experience heavy  psychological and emotional torture he  is tempted again to give up on life and  to become angry and jaded and perhaps he  does for a time but eventually we see  his true self emerge once again as he  one of the seven deadly sins as he makes  friends with Mellie Otis and the others  and as he struggles to overcome the loss  of Elaine even before Elaine is revived  we can see the growth and bonds  character by how he treats the people  around him including Mellie Otis Hawke  and Jericho but also King Elizabeth II  and so on even though he is haunted by  his tragic past and even though he feels  terrible guilt and despair bond still  treats others with compassion he still  jokes with them drinks with them  competes with them and laughs with them  despite everything he went through bond  is still a fundamentally good kind and  compassionate person and as the story  goes on this becomes more and more  evident I don't want to spoil too much  for those of you who haven't read the  manga  although the manga is amazing and I  definitely recommend checking it out but  bond eventually develops a technique  that is able to give energy to other  people rather than merely steal the  energy of others and of course stealing  objects and even the power of other  individuals was the fox's scent of  Reid's original special ability but as  he learns this new technique that gives  rather than taking away the development  of bonds physical power mirrors his  development as a character I think that  the seven deadly sins story handles  bonds development perfectly and he is  truly a multi-dimensional and nuanced  character that I cannot help but love he  starts off as an eccentric and  mysterious antihero with a dark past but  he becomes a full-fledged hero a  dedicated lover a faithful friend and an  all-around great person he might have a  reputation for being a greedy drunken  masochist and there is some truth to  these claims but bond is so much more  than that  he is a fictional character in a fantasy  Shonen anime / manga but he feels like a  real person because his character is so  well written and so thoroughly developed  and let's face it he also has an amazing  and utterly badass character design but  that's not quite as important all in all  bond this greedy drunken masochist is  one of my favorite anime characters of  all time he feels like a complete  complex and relatable individuals  someone we would all love to have a beer  with but at the same  time I wouldn't be afraid to shut a tear  over his heartbreaking past and his  unbreakable determination to keep moving  forward and that is why we all love bond  if you enjoyed this video and you want  to see more you can leave a like to let  me know if you're new to the channel  don't forget to subscribe and hit that  notification bell and finally I want to  say a big thank you to everyone who has  been supporting anime up or on patreon  both now and in the past if you want to  support more content on this channel  feel free to check out our patreon page  link in the description let me know what  you guys think about bond down in the  comments is he your favorite 7 Deadly  Sins character or do you prefer someone  else and feel free to hit me up on  Twitter and Instagram at anime uproar if  you have any requests for future videos  as always thank you guys so much for  watching and until next time see you  space cowboys  [Music]  you  [Music]

